From a8537fe78d7fd55958cb9364b5435cc10c00676f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hank Yeomans <hank@quorra.ah.local>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 11:55:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 48/61] kt_prefill: shared weight arenas replace the kt export
 (recipe T3.39 window 2 K2)

Rank 0 creates one sealed memfd per MoE layer sized by kt's weight_arena_bytes
and kt loads the compact CPU experts straight into it (kt patch 0003, MOEConfig
subclass injected around NativeMoEWrapper.load_weights); rank 1 maps the same
memfd through /proc/<pid0>/fd/<fd>; every rank cudaHostRegisters its mapping.
Streamed prefill then copies each rank's TP slice with cudaMemcpy2DAsync on a
side stream behind the previous layer's GEMM event: no kt export, no shm, no
gloo barriers, staging set reduced to w13/s13/w2/s2.

PrefillPipeline is now staged/layer_begin/layer_end over one staging set;
ArenaLayout.from_kt checks kt's carve (one TP part, E8M0 scales, constant
stride). KtRuntime.weight_arena_bytes / load_cpu_experts(weight_arena=) own
the kt side; kt_ep_wrapper creates the arena before the rank-0 load and
attaches all ranks after it.

