-before it is overwritten. 0 (default) disables the feature.
+each rank DMAs its TP slice of every CPU expert straight out of kt-kernel's
+resident weight storage into a per-rank staging set laid out for the
+FlashInfer SM120 CUTLASS MoE, and the layer runs the fused kernel twice: once
+over the resident GPU experts and once over the staged CPU experts.
+
+kt-kernel's resident storage is a caller-owned *arena* (kt patch 0003,
+``MOEConfig.weight_arenas``): rank 0 creates one ``memfd`` per MoE layer,
+sized by ``weight_arena_bytes``, and hands it to kt before the layer loads;
+kt carves every expert's gate / up / down block out of it (row-major MXFP4
+nibbles followed by the per-32 E8M0 scales, ``weight_arena_layout``). Rank 1
+maps the same memfd through ``/proc/<pid0>/fd/<n>``; every rank page-locks
+its mapping once (``cudaHostRegister``). From then on a streamed layer costs
+the host nothing: no export, no shared buffer, no barrier -- the copies are
+issued on a side stream against kt's own bytes and overlap the next layer's
+attention and resident-expert work. Before this (E22 .. T3.39 window 1) each
+layer-chunk paid a 65 ms core-bound kt export into a shared pinned buffer plus
+copies serialised with the compute stream.
+
+Decode and short chunks keep the CPU path untouched (kt reads the same arena).
+0 (default) disables the feature.
 
